// Where the recipes are kept:  in this browser, so no server is involved.
// To keep them elsewhere, change this ONE line.  With "yarn tsx scripts/recipe-servers.ts" running, try:
//   family cookbook is a folder at "http://127.0.0.1:4791/api/places/recipes"
//   family cookbook is a live room at "http://127.0.0.1:4791/api/rooms/recipes"
family cookbook is this device

a "recipe" is a view:
	- it is saved in the family cookbook
	- its "title" is text
	- its "servings" is a number
	- to draw it:
		<ui-form value={it} class="recipe">
			<ui-input name="title" aria-label="Recipe"/>
			<ui-text class="servings">serves {its servings}</ui-text>
			<ui-button class="remove" onClick={remove it}>Remove</ui-button>
		</ui-form>
	- to remove it:
		- undone as "Remove Recipe"
		remove it from the recipes

recipe box is an app:
	- its "search" is text
	- its "draft" is text
	- its "matches" is every recipe where its title includes the search, sorted by its title
	- to add the draft:
		if the draft is "" return
		add (a new recipe with title = the draft, servings = 2) to the recipes
		clear the draft
	- to draw it:
		<ui-form value={it} class="box">
			<ui-input name="draft" class="draft" label="New recipe" aria-label="New recipe"/>
			<ui-button class="add" disabled={the draft is ""} onClick={add the draft}>Add</ui-button>
			<ui-input name="search" class="search" label="Search" aria-label="Search"/>
		</ui-form>
		for each recipe in the matches
			draw the recipe
		while waiting:
			<ui-loader class="waiting"/>
		if there are none:
			<ui-text class="none">{"No recipes yet. Add the first one." if the search is "" otherwise "No recipes match your search."}</ui-text>
		if that fails:
			<ui-message class="failed" color="red">
				Can't reach the cookbook right now.
				<ui-button class="again" onClick={try again}>Try again</ui-button>
			</ui-message>

start the recipe box
